# Special relativity 03 — Threshold energies from E² = (pc)² + (mc²)²
#
# (Taylor & Wheeler, "Spacetime Physics", Ch. 7 (momenergy); Griffiths,
# "Introduction to Elementary Particles", Ch. 3 (relativistic kinematics).)  The invariant mass of a
# system, M c² = √(E_tot² − (p_tot c)²), is the same in every frame.  At
# threshold the products are made at rest in the centre-of-momentum frame, so
# M equals the sum of the product masses.
#
#  (a) The Bevatron (1955) made antiprotons by  p + p → p + p + p + p̄  with a
#      proton beam on a fixed hydrogen target.  What beam kinetic energy is
#      needed?  (Exact: K = 6 m_p c².)  Find it by solving the invariant-mass
#      condition for the beam energy, using E² = (pc)² + (mc²)² for the beam.
#  (b) Pion photoproduction γ + p → p + π⁰ on protons at rest.
#      (Exact: E_γ = ((m_p + m_π)² − m_p²) c² / 2 m_p.)
#  (c) The GZK cutoff: a cosmic-ray proton meets a head-on CMB photon of
#      energy 6.4×10⁻⁴ eV and makes a Δ⁺(1232).  Minimum proton energy?
#      (Exact for E_p ≫ m_p c²: E_p = (m_Δ² − m_p²) c⁴ / 4 E_γ.)

m_pi = 134.9768 MeV/c²       # (m_π can't be used as a name: see FRICTION.md)
m_Δ = 1232 MeV/c²
mp = m_p c²                   # proton rest energy

# (a) beam of total energy E on a proton at rest
p_beam(E) = √(E² - mp²) / c
M_inv(E) = √((E + mp)² - (p_beam(E) c)²) / c²
solve M_inv(E) = 4 m_p for E from mp to 100 GeV
print "(a) beam kinetic energy =", E - mp in GeV to 10 digits, "  6 m_p c² =", 6 mp in GeV to 10 digits
print "    beam momentum =", p_beam(E) in GeV/c to 10 digits

# (b) photon (E = pc) on a proton at rest
solve √((Eγ + mp)² - Eγ²) = (m_p + m_pi) c² for Eγ from 0 MeV to 1 GeV
print "(b) photon threshold =", Eγ in MeV to 10 digits, "  formula", ((m_p + m_pi)² - m_p²) c² / (2 m_p) in MeV to 10 digits

# (c) head-on collision: the momenta subtract.  Written as
# (E + E_γ)² − (pc − E_γ)² the two squares (~10⁴⁰ eV²) cancel to 1 part in 10²²
# and the answer is noise, so expand it first:  s = (m_p c²)² + 2 E_γ (E + pc).
E_cmb = 6.4e-4 eV
p_p(E) = √(E² - mp²) / c
solve mp² + 2 E_cmb (E_p + p_p(E_p) c) = (m_Δ c²)² for E_p from mp to 1e22 eV
print "(c) GZK threshold =", E_p in eV to 6 digits, "  approx", (m_Δ² - m_p²) c⁴ / (4 E_cmb) in eV to 6 digits
